The touchstone is actually an interesting idea; getting a plus or two
added to your weapons, or identifying some likely useful items, can be
worth a lot in the early game. (Especially if you have a dagger stack ---
you can pay to enchant all of it at once!)

Achieving a wishless ascension in Slash'EM may be easier for some
race/class combinations, at least, than in vanilla; Slash'EM just has
so much more total loot in the dungeon.

>      A few other likely choices:  amulet of flying to guard
> against having a trap door drop you into the midst of trouble,
> or a silver weapon to take care of the inevitable werecritters on
> the mall level.  Magic candle is another possibility.  Spellbook
> of magic missile is great too; that spell is very potent and in
> slash'em you can trivially prevent it from ever timing out.  Or
> blessed potions of gain ability; high constitution means extra
> hit points whenever you gain a level so getting it early means
> you'll have the bonus more times overall.

While all of these seem useful, I wouldn't spend a wish on any except
maybe magic missile in the early game; with MR, reflection, and negative
AC on DL:1, werecreatures and trap doors aren't really major threats. (In
fact I'd never considered spending a wish to be protected from trap
doors before. If you are really afraid of trap doors, hit the 's' key
often.) I'd be preparing for the mid- and end-game at that point, and
would want to make wishes that stayed useful into the endgame. Magic
candle would be replaced by magic lamp, silver weapon would likely be
replaced by an artifact, blessed potions of gain ability would be found
later. Some people might wear an amulet of flying in the endgame to deal
with pools but I personally wouldn't imagine that as kit.

High constitution does mean high hit points but it's so easy to alchemize
thirty blessed potions of full healing in Slash'EM so why bother?

Another thing to consider: Athame. (Magicbane would be my choice, but
the OP says no artifact wishes. In Slash'EM you can even dual-wield
Magicbane with some other artifact --- how could you turn that down?)
Elbereth remains immensely powerful.

>      They're all things you'll find eventually, but having one or
