This is an important intangible --- if having the amulet of lifesaving
means that you play poorly, don't wish for the amulet of lifesaving. I
don't get that effect, and it protects me from all sorts of things,
though only once. I'd pass on figurines to acquire angelic pets too,
but for any player, because they are only 80% going to provide you an
angelic pet, and I am not going to let a wand-on-DL1 game hinge on a
dieroll, I am going to win.

